Fix loading of mingw-w64 CRT import libraries in the RTS linker, which
broke GHCi, Template Haskell and runghc with mingw-w64 14:

  libmingwex.a: unknown symbol `__imp___msvcrt_assert'

mingw-w64 imports __msvcrt_assert from api-ms-win-crt-runtime-l1-1-0.dll,
which exports it as _assert.

 * Honour the short import name type (NO_PREFIX, UNDECORATE, EXPORTAS) as
   described in the PE/COFF spec. llvm-dlltool emits EXPORTAS for renamed
   imports such as __msvcrt_assert.
 * binutils' dlltool emits a member defining __imp___msvcrt_assert with the
   hint name _assert. Register the symbol name too, and look imports up in
   the DLL by the hint name rather than by the symbol name.
 * Resolve a reference to the IAT slot __imp_foo through the symbol table
   when an import library already provided foo, instead of searching the
   DLLs for an export named foo.
 * checkAndLoadImportLibrary freed the buffer holding the symbol name (and
   the DLL name) before inserting it into the symbol table, which keeps a
   pointer to its key, so later lookups of import library symbols failed.
 * lookupSymbol_PEi386 passed the caller's type pointer to the lookup of
   the _head symbol of a BFD import, overwriting SYM_TYPE_CODE with
   SYM_TYPE_DATA on the first lookup. A call to e.g. wcsncmp from
   libucrt.a then went through a data jump island and crashed with
   "Access violation in generated code when executing data" (any file
   IO in GHCi on UCRT64).

